ext-align: center; height: 55px; width: 102.611px; padding: 10px !important;\">\n<div>Product ID</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 166.056px; padding: 10px !important;\">\n<div>Connector Model</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 118.611px; padding: 10px !important;\">Length(mm)</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 206.403px; padding: 10px !important;\">Outer Diameter (mm)</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 112.236px; padding: 10px !important;\">Wire Gauge</td>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; text-align: center; height: 23px; width: 102.611px; padding: 10px !important;\">PD001</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 23px; width: 166.056px; padding: 10px !important;\">\n<div data-lark-html-role=\"root\"><span data-eleid=\"5\">XH2.54 - PH2.0</span></div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 23px; width: 118.611px; padding: 10px !important;\">200</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 23px; width: 206.403px; padding: 10px !important;\">1.6</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 23px; width: 112.236px; padding: 10px !important;\">22AWG</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"text-align: left;\">Consideration</h2>\n<p> </p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 7.4V power supply is incompatible with devices that require lower operating voltages, such as the ​Lithophane LED Backlight Board, the ​N20 Dual Shaft Worm Gear Motor (model LA009)​, and ​COB LED Strip Lights.</li>\n<li>​Before use, always verify the compatible voltage range listed in the product details page for your specific device.​</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "This cable enables the connection between the 14500 7.4V 800mAh Li-ion Battery - PC003 and the 4 Channels Power Distribution Board (PDB) - IA005, as well as components such as the 100mm Y-Type PH2.0 to Dual SH1.0 Conversion Wire-XC003, delivering a portable, high-capacity power solution.\n\nThe 7.4V power supply is incompatible with devices that require lower operating voltages, such as the ​Lithophane LED Backlight Board, the ​N20 Dual Shaft Worm Gear Motor (model LA009)​, and ​COB LED Strip Lights.\n\n​Before use, always verify the compatible voltage range listed in the product details page for your specific device.​",
